        "original_id": "6b1bb38f-5791-5005-aa0e-f09c9fada47b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Trade unions in the United Kingdom, Labour Party, Labour Representation Committee, National Policy Forum\n- People: Tony Blair\n- Concepts: Trade union movement, policy-making system, Partnership in Power\n\nFacts:\n- Trade unions in the United Kingdom were legalised in 1871.\n- The trade union movement in Britain sought to reform socio-economic conditions for working men in British industries.\n- The trade unions' search for reform led to the creation of the Labour Representation Committee.\n- The Labour Representation Committee effectively formed the basis for today's Labour Party.\n- The Labour Party still has extensive links with the Trade Union Movement in Britain.\n- Tony Blair was born on 6 May 1953.\n- Tony Blair served as Leader of the Labour Party from 21 July 1994 to 24 June 2007.\n- The National Policy Forum of the British Labour Party was set up by Tony Blair as part of the Partnership in Power process.\n- Tony Blair served as Prime Minister of the United Kingdom from 2 May 1997 to 27 June 2007.\n- The National Policy Forum is part of the policy-making system of the Labour Party.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
